# tests/threads — MIT #15-A kernel threads (weeks 3–4)

Stub created week 2 (design gate). Programs land in `user/` as written; this file
tracks the planned set + pass criteria.

## Planned tests

- `t-smoke`: parent + one child thread print distinct messages from separate kstacks;
  verified in GDB (break `swtch`, confirm distinct `sp` + shared `pagetable`).
- `t-counter`: N threads × M increments on shared counter with user spinlock; final
  value exact.
- `t-pipe`: producer/consumer threads through a pipe using `thread_yield`; no lost
  items, no deadlock.
- `t-churn`: create/join loop (N=8 threads × 100 rounds); no kstack leak (free-frame
  count returns to start).

## Pass criteria

All four complete under `CPUS=1` and `CPUS=2` with exact expected output; free-frame
count stable across `t-churn`; main-thread exit during live children tears down
cleanly (decision D1); `fork()` from multithreaded proc returns -1 (decision D2).
